<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Browning-Ferris cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Browning-Ferris cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gruntal &amp; Co said it downgraded Browning-Ferris Industries Inc to sell from hold.</p>
<p>-- despite the downgrade, said raised the fiscal 1997 earnings estimate to $1.62 a share from $1.50 a share and the fiscal 1998 estimate to $1.86 a share from $1.65 a share.</p>
<p>-- said &quot;we do not believe investors can justify paying close to 20x earnings for a stock that can, at best, sustain operating earnings growth of 10 percent.&quot;</p>
<p>-- said 12-month price target is $26 to $28.</p>
<p>-- Browning-Ferris gained 1/4 to 35.</p>
